  "id": "Compound::DB01039 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Fenofibrate exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c9 and Cyp3a4, both of which are involved in oxidoreductive activities that involve quinone or similar compound acceptors. These pathways are closely linked to Cyp2c8, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Fenofibrate may influence its activity. The observed binding to Cyp2c9 and Cyp3a4, which are both part of the same functional category, implies that Fenofibrate may modulate the activity of Cyp2c8 through these shared pathways. The evidence suggests that Fenofibrate could act as a substrate or inhibitor of Cyp2c8, potentially altering its metabolic capacity. The integration of these pathways supports a mechanistic link between Fenofibrate and Cyp2c8, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple binding and functional pathways across different cytochrome P450 isoforms underscores the complexity of the metabolic interactions involved.",
